  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP South Sudan Climate Security Mechanism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Climate and Security Mechanism is a joint initiative between the Department of Political and Peacebuilding Affairs (DPPA), United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) and United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP) aiming to strengthen the capacity of the UN system to analyse and address the adverse impacts of climate change on peace and security. Ireland&#x2019;s grant supports a dedicated Senior Climate and Security Advisor based in Juba, South Sudan. This Advisor will facilitate the drafting of the UNMISS-UN Country Team Climate and Security Strategy, and enhance coordination between UNMISS, UNCT, and other partners. Through this Grant, Ireland became a member of the Climate Security Mechanism, along with Sweden, Germany, Norway and the UK.</narrative>
  </description>
